# This package is an application, so the pin is the newest interpreter
# every dependency installs on, a release candidate counting (section 1
# of the organization's standard). It declares no dependency yet, so the
# pin is the newest Python released; the pull request that declares the
# first dependency checks the pin against it. It is also the newest the
# test matrix covers. requires-python names the floor, and both linters
# are aimed at that end deliberately -- ruff infers its target from
# requires-python, and pyproject.toml's [tool.mypy] pins python_version
# to match it.
#
# A whole-line comment only: uv skips one of these, but a trailing comment
# on the version line makes it ignore the file and fall back to a default
# interpreter.
